{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012tmotp7q9WgCy2EecaZ8wV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough context to produce the planning artifacts. Let me also quickly check the docs/02_planning/README.md and docs/05_acceptance_tests/README.md.\n\nActually, I have enough information. Let me now create the planning artifacts.\n\n**Summary of what I know:**\n\n### Current state\n`Backtest.__init__` stores:\n- `self.position_sizer = components.position_sizer` — NEVER called directly from Backtest methods\n- `self.risk_manager = components.risk_manager` — called in `run()` (line 256) and `run_replay()` (line 373): `self.risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()`\n\n\n- `self.broker = components.broker` — NEVER called directly from Backtest methods\n- `self.order_manager = components.order_manager` — called in `_analyze_and_trade()` and `_replay_and_trade()`\n\nAdditionally, `backtest.py` has calls to `self.order_manager.close_trade(...)` at lines 423 and 653, but that method doesn't exist in `OrderManager`. The `OrderManager` already has `risk_manager` as an internal attribute.\n\n### Changes needed\n\n**`quantagent/trading/order_manager.py`** needs two new methods: a `reset_daily_tracker()` method and a `close_trade()` method to handle the missing functionality that Backtest is trying to call.\n\n**`quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`** needs to remove the direct component assignments for `position_sizer`, `risk_manager`, and `broker`, then update the calls to `reset_daily_tracker()` and `close_trade()` to route through `order_manager` instead.\n\nFor the tests, I need to verify that `OrderManager.reset_daily_tracker()` properly delegates to the risk manager, that `close_trade()` executes correctly, and that `Backtest` no longer holds those three attributes directly.\n\nLooking at how `close_trade` is called in `Backtest` with the trade ID and current price, I need to make sure the `OrderManager` implementation can handle looking up the trade and executing the close order properly. I need to figure out what `close_trade` should actually do. Looking at the Trade model, it has `exit_price`, `closed_at`, and `pnl` fields that need to be set when closing. The method signature from backtest.py shows it takes a trade ID and current price, and should return an Order. So the implementation needs to create an opposing order through the broker and update the Trade record with the exit details.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2489,"cache_read_input_tokens":66113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2489},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba6b8a9-0956-46b4-a5ab-2f80c3a37c45","uuid":"e21c16b7-a450-495d-9673-091960e2a274"}
